          <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/national-minimum-wage-rates" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 font-semibold">GOV.UK — National Minimum Wage rates</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/tax-codes" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 font-semibold">GOV.UK — Understanding your tax code</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Update Schedule</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Wagecheck updates its calculators every April when the new tax year begins. This is when HMRC publishes updated income tax bands, National Insurance thresholds, student loan repayment thresholds and other rates. We review and apply all changes within the first week of the new tax year. Outside of the annual update, we correct any errors or misinterpretations as soon as they are identified. Each calculator page includes a change log so you can see exactly when rates were last updated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
